Original ADA source packages were adapted from personalrobotics/ada_ros2,
Personal Robotics Laboratory, BSD-3-Clause. Their original copyright notices,
licenses and robot assets are preserved in the local development archive.
Source: https://github.com/personalrobotics/ada_ros2
Snapshot: 563d6e0e460f081ecad4e6bbfd32f937c7998d30 (October 12, 2026).
The distributed runtime consists of jaco_vla and jaco_vla_interfaces, including
a new Cartesian endpoint using the Kinova SDK. Robot description, IMU,
camera-extrinsics, MoveIt and ros2_control packages are archived locally under
the Git-ignored .dev/ directory and are not part of the distributed runtime.

Camera serials, calibration, frame/joint names, protocol keys and the legacy
10D state mapping are from the supplied notes and inspected setup.
The new VLA client is separate from the upstream client.
ROS and the separately installed Kinova SDK retain their own licenses.
LeRobot was used as a conceptual reference only; no LeRobot code is bundled.
